{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"19a78bee-bf2d-48ff-95fd-a28e160280d1","step_index":11,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"`middleware/` (various middlewares)\n- `_examples/` (example programs)\n- Tests covering routing, middleware, and utilities.\n\n**Goal**\n\nAdd support for path‑prefix patterns of the form `METHOD /path/*` (wildcard after a slash) to the routing API (`Handle` and `HandleFunc`). This requires:\n\n1. Updating the pattern parsing logic to recognise the `*` suffix as a prefix matcher.\n2. Adjusting the internal routing tables so that a prefix pattern matches any request whose path starts with the given prefix.\n3. Ensuring both `Handle` (which registers a `http.Handler`) and `HandleFunc` (which registers a handler function) use the same parsing rules.\n4. Adding unit tests that verify:\n   - Exact method+path works as before.\n   - Prefix pattern matches deeper paths.\n   - Non‑matching methods or paths are correctly rejected.\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- The existing routing implementation already parses patterns like `\"GET /foo\"` into method and path components.  \n- Prefix handling can be expressed by storing the prefix (without the trailing `*`) and performing a `strings.HasPrefix` check during route lookup.  \n- No external network access is required; all changes will be made locally and tested with `go test ./...`.\n\n**Next steps**\n\n1. Locate the pattern parsing code (likely in `chi.go` or a helper file).  \n2. Extend it to detect a trailing `*` and mark the route as a prefix route.  \n3. Modify the request lookup (`route.Match` or similar) to handle prefix routes.  \n4. Update `Handle` and `HandleFunc` wrappers to use the new parsing logic.  \n5. Add tests in `router_test.go` (or a new test file) that register prefix routes and verify matching behavior.  \n\nI will now examine the routing source files to identify where patterns are parsed.\n","duration_seconds":5.819359,"usage":{"input_tokens":4172,"output_tokens":556,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":5120,"total_tokens":4728}}}
